[size=5][b]NATIVE ELDEN RING UI FOR YOUR MOD[/b][/size]

One shared menu host. Multiple client mods. No overlay.

[url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI][b]GITHUB: SOURCE, SDK, DOCUMENTATION AND EXAMPLES[/b][/url]
[url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI/releases/latest]COMPLETE WINDOWS SDK AND RUNTIME RELEASE[/url][/center]

[quote][b]ERNativeUI is primarily an SDK for mod authors.[/b]

It lets a client mod add native menus, settings, dialogs, text input, color pickers and configurable input bindings without owning another competing set of Elden Ring UI hooks.

[b]Players install one canonical ERNativeUI.dll host.[/b] If a mod lists ERNativeUI as a requirement, download the host from this page's Files tab, install it once, and let every compatible client mod connect to that same copy.[/quote]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10767/10767-1788711693-1080782593.png[/img][/center]
[center][size=5][b]ONE NATIVE HOST, MULTIPLE CLIENT MODS[/b][/size][/center]

ERNativeUI owns the process-wide native hooks and safely merges UI registered by independent client DLLs. Players get one consistent native experience; mod authors get a reusable public API instead of rediscovering and maintaining the same game internals in every project.

[list]
[*][b]Looks native[/b] - uses Elden Ring's own GFX controls, focus, help text, transitions, dialogs and Back navigation.
[*][b]Works together[/b] - several client mods can contribute menus through one shared host DLL.
[*][b]Built for mod authors[/b] - stable C11 binary ABI plus a friendly header-only C++17 wrapper.
[*][b]Compiler friendly[/b] - no client import library and no STL, exception or allocator ownership shared across DLL boundaries.
[*][b]Versioned for compatibility[/b] - compatible 1.x hosts retain the earlier published 1.x API contracts used by existing clients.
[*][b]Game-update conscious[/b] - signatures and object boundaries are validated before native hooks are installed.
[*][b]Open and reproducible[/b] - source, tests, examples, GFX tooling and reverse-engineering notes are public.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10767/10767-1788711381-1678734545.png[/img]
[i]Settings from multiple client mods, merged into Elden Ring's native Game Options page.[/i][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10767/10767-1788711733-1600560216.png[/img][/center]
[center][size=5][b]FEATURES[/b][/size][/center]

[b]Native controls[/b]
[list]
[*]Button and nested Submenu
[*]Toggle and bounded Slider
[*]Inline Choice and native Popup Choice list
[*]TextInput with placeholder, confirmed-value callbacks and configurable length
[*]ColorPicker with native palette and custom RGB editor
[/list]

[b]Menus and pages[/b]
[list]
[*]Add rows to supported built-in Configuration pages: Game Options, Camera Options, Display, Sound, Network, Keyboard/Mouse and Graphics
[*]Create client-owned submenus
[*]Automatic capacity detection and pagination
[*]Native Next, Previous and Back behavior
[*]Automatic page numbering and customizable provider-submenu titles
[/list]

[b]Dialogs, localization and configuration[/b]
[list]
[*]Native modal alerts with dismiss-only, one-button or two-button layouts
[*]Bottom or centered dialog placement
[*]Runtime detection of Elden Ring's selected Steam language
[*]Localized ERNativeUI navigation labels with an English fallback
[*]Provider-owned INI storage and a public input-assignment codec
[/list]

[b]Player-configurable input bindings[/b]
[list]
[*]Register controller, keyboard and mouse actions
[*]Show those actions in Elden Ring's native Button Settings and Key Bindings screens
[*]Receive callbacks when the player activates an action
[*]Observe assignment and Clear changes so client mods can persist them
[/list]

